D-PHRG.1 ruled Path A (pandoc) over Path B (custom markdown→HTML
conversion script in framework/tools/loam/). Path A is cheaper to
ship (~30s install + ~2s regen), uses standard tooling, and the
markdown is structurally vanilla GFM (tables + lists + emphasis +
code spans + ordered/unordered lists; NO code fences, footnotes, or
task lists per pre-source-edit grep). Path B would have added 1.5-3h
of authoring + maintenance overhead for negligible reproducibility
gain — pandoc is widely available across systems and the brew
install is one line. Path B captured as new FIDRAFT
F-PAPER-REGEN-CUSTOM-SCRIPT for follow-on if a future scenario
surfaces value (e.g., system without pandoc; reproducibility gate
needing zero system-tool dependencies).

